WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.079
(coin clinking)

00:00:02.079 --> 00:00:04.611
- All the machines in
this arcade are homemade.

00:00:04.611 --> 00:00:07.469
There's something magical about all this.

00:00:07.469 --> 00:00:10.061
As a child, I found that
making things that made people

00:00:10.061 --> 00:00:13.708
laugh was satisfying and seemed
more point in doing that

00:00:13.708 --> 00:00:16.044
than making useful machines.

00:00:16.044 --> 00:00:18.877
(whimsical music)

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.059
I'm Tim Hunkin, and I'm a
cartoonist and engineer.

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:29.510
I have two arcades, one
on the coast on the pier,

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.921
and this one in central London
called Novelty Automation.

00:00:33.921 --> 00:00:37.620
In total, I suppose I've
made about 50 machines.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.731
Not many people have that
as their ambition in life,

00:00:40.731 --> 00:00:43.001
but yeah, it suits me.

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:44.590
This is Pet or Meat.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:48.170
You spin the wheel, and you
find if the lamb ends up

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:52.601
sitting with you on the sofa,
or being carved for dinner.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.501
It was a hobby that got out of control.

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:55.901
This is Autofrisk.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.793
You stand in front here,
the gloves inflate,

00:00:58.793 --> 00:01:01.043
and then they pat you down.

00:01:01.892 --> 00:01:04.931
Britain's got a great history
of satire, and I suppose

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.639
I'm not really particularly
political myself, but I think

00:01:08.639 --> 00:01:11.353
it's healthy for little people to poke fun

00:01:11.353 --> 00:01:12.951
at the rich and powerful.

00:01:12.951 --> 00:01:17.172
You fly this little drone round
this Beverly Hills mansion,

00:01:17.172 --> 00:01:20.222
and see all the stars
inside, and you're paparazzi.

00:01:20.222 --> 00:01:22.193
You have to try and take
the photos to fill up

00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:23.953
the cover of the magazine.

00:01:23.953 --> 00:01:25.386
- [Game] You're all under arrest.

00:01:25.386 --> 00:01:27.081
(camera shutter clicks)

00:01:27.081 --> 00:01:29.121
- I get my ideas from lots of places.

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:31.412
It's partly things happening
in my life, partly things

00:01:31.412 --> 00:01:35.760
happening in the news, and
partly from old arcade machines

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.772
and mechanisms.

00:01:36.772 --> 00:01:37.812
This is Test Your Nerve.

00:01:37.812 --> 00:01:41.881
You have to put your hand
inside the cage with the mad dog

00:01:41.881 --> 00:01:43.329
for as long as you dare.

00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:44.619
(game growling)

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:47.290
To do something like this,
you have to enjoy the process

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:48.970
of making things.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.781
I spent most of my life solving
conventional engineering

00:01:51.781 --> 00:01:54.170
problems, rather than
thinking up the jokes.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.040
(laughing)

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.460
This is the Chiropodist.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.221
You have to take off
your shoe for this one.

00:01:58.221 --> 00:02:00.800
You put your foot in the
treatment bay down the bottom,

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.050
and it feels really weird.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:06.861
Seeing people enjoying, using
the machines, keeps me at it.

00:02:06.861 --> 00:02:09.250
And also, because they
take money, it provides

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.770
me income to let me keep at it.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.666
So to me, it's a pretty perfect system.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.226
It sure beats working.

00:02:15.226 --> 00:02:17.865
- [Game] Good morning, sir.

00:02:17.865 --> 00:02:20.906
- I never planned my career
or anything about my life.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.626
It's just occasionally a
sort of opportunity comes up,

00:02:23.626 --> 00:02:27.986
and then I go for it. (laughing)

00:02:27.986 --> 00:02:30.819
(munching sounds)

